{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795379800,"nonce":"NGfaxh8zx5zecfMWG7KkJoVctPY=","title":"Immix thread hooks do not build on Windows","message":"immix_heap exists only on unix. The hooks added for multi-thread collection called it without a cfg gate. These were pool_alloc (blocking, safepoint, attach), the band pool in zrtl.rs, and the embed runtime in promise.rs and host_futures.rs. Windows and wasm builds would fail to compile. The commits are unpushed, so CI has not seen them.\n\nFound by cargo check --tests --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc before the push. The wasm32 lint from the CI wasm job also passes after the fix.\n\nFix. host_heap has blocking, safepoint and attach, which call immix_heap on unix and do nothing elsewhere. The shared code calls them there.","files":null}]}